# Testing and Validation

The Smart Sea Belt prototype was tested in a controlled backwater environment to evaluate the operation of the developed system and its major safety functions.

## 1. Backwater Prototype Testing

The prototype was subjected to controlled testing in a backwater environment to observe system operation under water-based conditions.

### Tested Functions

| Test Area | Purpose | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Smart Watch | Verify wearable system operation | Tested |
| Heart-rate sensing | Verify sensor response | Tested |
| Motion sensing | Verify motion-related detection | Tested |
| SOS function | Verify emergency activation | Tested |
| BLE communication | Verify Smart Watch communication with Boat Hub | Tested |
| GPS | Verify location acquisition | Tested |
| Boat Hub | Verify central processing and communication | Tested |
| LoRa communication | Verify transmission toward Base Unit | Tested |
| Emergency alert | Verify emergency notification | Tested |
| Flotation mechanism | Verify controlled flotation response | Tested |
| Rudder mechanism | Verify controlled actuator response | Tested |

## 2. Testing Environment

The prototype was evaluated in a controlled backwater environment as part of the project's practical testing and validation activities.

The test focused on observing the prototype's functional behaviour and communication between the major system modules.

